{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489046-overpowered-theoretical-in-clan-discipline-combinations","id":1489046,"title":"Overpowered Theoretical In Clan Discipline Combinations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T19:40:04-07:00","id":1489046,"title":"Overpowered Theoretical In Clan Discipline Combinations","content":"What the title says. Come up with a [V20] three discipline spread to make your character a Combat Monster (assume 1-5 spread, but higher is fine).<br /> <br /> My pick is Auspex, Obtenebration, and Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> On its own, Obtenebration can carry the day. Combine Blood Boil and Tenebrous Form and you have something truly frightening. Shroud of Night or Arms of the Abyss and Theft of Vitae is also good. Auspex to counter sneak attacks and deliver the goods at a distance with Psychic Projection rounds this one out for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T20:49:50-07:00","id":1489055,"title":"","content":"Setite Sorcery, Protean, Auspex<br /> <br /> Setite sorcery because it is made up of 4 different Blood Magic Traditions, all which have some pretty cool uniqe paths and rituals. Presence because it is pretty useful when it comes to persuading others, especially those in large groups. Auspex because nobody wants to be unpleasently surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T01:47:44-07:00","id":1489071,"title":"","content":"I've long thought that the Nosferatu would be much better off with Animalism, Potence, and Protean in the place of Obfuscate. Dwelling underground as a clan stereotype is absurd if they don't have the native ability to see in the dark, the extra mobility could be a godsend for making sections of their tunnels inaccessible to others, and the stealth-and-illusions powers if Obfuscate trivializes the clan's weakness to begin with.<br /> <br /> I assume the only reason they don't have this combination by canon default is the combination of Potence with Feral Claws, which would make them the nastiest unarmed damage dealers in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T02:05:02-07:00","id":1489073,"title":"","content":"The toreador already have the best discipline lineup. The three disciplines cover all the bases at peak efficiency. In terms of raw combat brujah are best and psychic might Dominate malkavians dominate.<br /> <br /> Exotic disciplines don't tend to synergize very well due to heavy vitae expenditure and specialised skill set. I once watched a toreador ballet dancer demolish an angelis ater in single round of combat. Potence compliments obtenerbration way better than domanion.<br /> <br /> I imagine a lasombra with Fortitude instead of Dominate would be very bad news in a fight but celerity would mean it burns through blood too quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-04-2022, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T07:01:10-07:00","id":1489108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489046-overpowered-theoretical-in-clan-discipline-combinations?p=1489071#post1489071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've long thought that the Nosferatu would be much better off with Animalism, Potence, and Protean in the place of Obfuscate. Dwelling underground as a clan stereotype is absurd if they don't have the native ability to see in the dark, the extra mobility could be a godsend for making sections of their tunnels inaccessible to others, and the stealth-and-illusions powers if Obfuscate trivializes the clan's weakness to begin with.<br /> <br /> I assume the only reason they don't have this combination by canon default is the combination of Potence with Feral Claws, which would make them the nastiest unarmed damage dealers in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I like the old Greek Gangrel bloodline- Animalism, Obfuscate, Protean. They were dwelling in sewers long before the grubby Nosferatu got the idea, and were better at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T09:23:02-07:00","id":1489121,"title":"","content":"I'm partial to Auspex, Fortitude and Presence with Celerity on the side. A good combo for spotting trouble, defusing a situation and if you can't you can take a inhuman amount of punishment while hightailing out of there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-04-2022, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T11:06:10-07:00","id":1489136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489046-overpowered-theoretical-in-clan-discipline-combinations#post1489046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the title says. Come up with a [V20] three discipline spread to make your character a Combat Monster (assume 1-5 spread, but higher is fine).</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting concept, but I have to ask exactly how you are defining a &quot;Combat Monster&quot; and what kind of combat you are envisioning?<br /> <br /> Many people envision a combat monster as a character that has to be in direct combat proximity, can soak tons of damage and or do insane amounts of damage. Others envision a true combat monster build as one which negates the concept of direct combat by being able to attack at range. Conversely there are those that see the idea of being able to attack without risking yourself as a true combat monster.<br /> <br /> 1. The build is the standard Potence, Celerity, and Fortitude build with a melee weapon. You must get into direct combat to interact with the character. They soak everything, hit hard and often.<br /> <br /> 2. The build negates other builds by changing the rules of combat. For instance a Gargoyle with Obfuscate or any other vampire with Flight and Obfuscate that has a high caliber Sniper Rifle, a satchel of phosphorus grenades, and a radio head set is more or less immune to combat since it can engage up to two miles away, reposition as needed, and can change tactics based on the situation. With a little for thought you can even have multiple types of ammunition to suit different requirements.<br /> <br /> 3. The only thing that can defeat Necromancy is other Necromancy, so sending ghosts to set fires to your enemies haven at noon, means no one has any idea what happened, who did it, or why it happened. The enemy can not attack you because they don't know you exist as an opponent. So Necromancy, Dominate, and Resources 5 can destroy whole coteries without risking you being exposed, let alone drawing you into combat. But you could achieve similar results with Thaumaturgy Path of Technomancy, Dominate, and Resources 5 because hacking and drone swarms can get really scary.<br /> <br /> It all really depends on what your opponent's strengths are and how you choose to negate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T14:17:51-07:00","id":1489152,"title":"","content":"The wording isn't entirely clear so it depends on rullings, but this one's almost impossible to beat assuming you can caste Arms of the Abyss while in Tenebrous form. (i'm a little doubtful) <br /> <br /> Obtenebration 5 (abyss mysticism) <br /> Diamonion 6<br /> Thaumaturgical countermagic.<br /> <br /> You're a mass of darkness.<br /> You're immune to physical attacks <br /> You're immune to fire<br /> You're resistant against magic. <br /> You can feed through your tentacles. You never need to revert to human form. <br /> You have an extreme weakness to sunlight, but most can't exploit that weakness. <br /> <br /> Assuming that's Badwrong<br /> <br /> In the context of the limitations put out by the OP I need to mention that Diamonion 6 is just the ultimate power because it's <i>everything. </i>It's the power to give yourself a demonic investment. Is it XP efficient? Usually not. But you can give yourself any physical, mental, social, mystical or evem moral enhancement you want. Hell, Investments can permanently provide backgrounds. <br /> <br /> Baring that, being able to go incorporeal (say, protean) and still attack (Koldunism) is stronk. <br /> If we need to simplify further<br /> Auspex, Celerity, Potence. With the right equipment and skills, this is best. With these disciplines you should be able to mitigate the disadvantages of armour completely, compensating for your lack of Fortitude. You're good at detecting and escaping danger, and you're almost guaranteed to strike first and decisively. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T09:48:56-07:00","id":1489240,"title":"","content":"Animalism, Auspex, Vicissitude is good enough for me.<br /> <br /> They can\u2019t hide from you, can\u2019t get the drop on you, almost always have multi-target penalties trying to deal with your heavily-modified face-eating pets, and even coming at you one-on-one you have an off-brand Crinos Shape.<br /> <br /> Sounds nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T11:15:22-07:00","id":1489250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Garygeneric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489046-overpowered-theoretical-in-clan-discipline-combinations?p=1489240#post1489240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animalism, Auspex, Vicissitude is good enough for me.<br /> <br /> They can\u2019t hide from you, can\u2019t get the drop on you, almost always have multi-target penalties trying to deal with your heavily-modified face-eating pets, and even coming at you one-on-one you have an off-brand Crinos Shape.<br /> <br /> Sounds nice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting combo for sure Garygeneric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T04:24:09-07:00","id":1489313,"title":"","content":"I had fun brainstorming a few with my ST a few years back. Combination Disciplines get pretty good so I think most of the suggestions here wouldn't be just theoretical. <br /> (Like, I think Retain the Quick Blood was the best part of my Assamite character and it wasn't even something I created)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Retain the Quick Blood<br /> Celerity 3, Quietus (Cruscitus) 2<br /> Assamite Warriors who have achieved some mastery<br /> over both Celerity and Cruscitus have learned how to hone<br /> their blood to more efficient means. With this power, the<br /> vampire recovers blood spent to activate Celerity.<br /> System: Any blood spent to buy extra actions through<br /> Celerity returns to the vampire\u2019s blood pool as if it had<br /> never been used at a rate of one per minute. Once learned,<br /> this power is considered always active. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T09:17:55-07:00","id":1489338,"title":"","content":"Now for say for what I consider overpowered discipline combos.<br /> <br /> Mine would be Fortitude, Potence and Protean if I was a combat heavy monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T16:19:07-07:00","id":1490074,"title":"","content":"Assuming a 1-5 spread, the most powerful discipline combination for combat exclusively would be Chimerstry, Temporis, and Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> For defense Obtenebration is completely unnecessarily as the level 3 ritual, Incorporeal Passage, makes you immune to all physical damage, in essence blocking everything except mental, metaphysical, or sunlight based attacks.<br /> <br /> For offense Horrid Reality is in essence the best attack in the game as it deals UNSOAKABLE lethal damage, and the enemy CANNOT escape it once it is cast, thus making it a form of certain unconsciousness, followed by swift death.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Thaumaturgy Path of Warding grants potentially 11 (with Willpower) extra aggravated damage, or more if it stacks, by warding an item, which on a single weapon is devastating. Additionally, The Unquenchable Flame of Mars ritual makes your weapon aggravated normally, so that's very nice.<br /> <br /> Another form of offense is directly through Focused Mind and Theft of Vitae as once a (living) target is depleted of blood points, they die immediately, therefore there is no need to bypass additional health levels, or other forms of defense besides completely draining a (living) target's pool of blood.<br /> <br /> Temporis however seals their fate completely by removing actions, and allowing us to take additional casting actions, thus being able to drain over 50 blood points per turn or attacking several times with Cauldron of Blood, or using Horrid Reality multiple times.<br /> <br /> We have passively a remarkably high initiative with a constant 10 dexterity due to Blood Pump and Blood of Potency, as well as a starting Wits of 5.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, we can always with Path of Conjuration 5, or simply with Asymmetrical Reproduction ritual, gain 2 additional allies to cast the Dur-An-Ki ritual Bound By Oath, which can be cast as Rites of the Blood declares that all rituals of different blood magic sects can be cast by one another with proper adaptation, thus allowing us to ALWAYS win initiative.<br /> <br /> Upon winning initiative we can throw them into a Horrid Reality, if multiple people are fighting, then conjuring a grain of antimatter should do the trick (dealing large amounts of UNSOAKABLE aggravated damage according to the Sons of Ether Tradition Book Revised in MICROSCOPIC amounts, which you can conjure in HUMAN SIZED amounts because of the Path of Conjuration), or if you wish not to take advice from the Etherites or House Flambeau and blow everything in a ~2060 mile radius to pieces, then Cauldron of Blood, which kills a mortal with a single level of aggravated damage (mortal, supposedly meaning living, although one could argue that since ghouls can survive if they soak ALL the aggravated damage, then werewolves, mages, changelings, etc... could also survive if ALL damage is soaked) should do the trick, especially if cast 10 times due to Temporis, or we can simply attack with our sword which deals either +11 levels, or infinite levels, of aggravated damage due to the ward.<br /> <br /> This will kill any vampire, werewolf, or changeling out there. However what if we're fighting Wraiths, Mages, Tremere and / or Lasombra.<br /> <br /> For Wraiths, using Giovanni or Cappadocian rituals since Rites of the Blood allows us to do that with Thaumaturgy fixes the problem. Spirits also aren't an issue due to Spirit Manipulation.<br /> <br /> The Tremere can simply be defeated by Horrid Reality as it's a mental assault and thus bypasses Incorporeal Passage, and the Lasombra can be beaten in the same fashion, or by just removing all of their shadow using Lure of Flames.<br /> <br /> Now when it comes to Mages life becomes a living hell, as any Forces 2 magus could just drain our kinetic energy and utterly immobilize us preventing us from harming them with our sword or Cauldron of Blood, rewind time with Time 3, or cast powerful mental attacks with Mind 3 / Life 3 / Matter 2, or conjure sunlight with Correspondence 4, as well as have layers of force fields and damage reducing effects that make them practically immortal.<br /> <br /> However, since we win initiative, we have no issue, as I always like to say, Mages deal with numbers whereas Vampires cheat. In essence even if the Mage had a +100 to their initiative through a powerful Time ritual they still couldn't beat us because we &quot;cheat&quot; and simply move to the top of initiative, rather than manipulating numbers.<br /> <br /> Now we also must have conjured Primium and be prepared to employ countermagick to deal with any possible offensive Time 4 hanging spells for when we act, but even then the only thing that can truly stop us would be a Time 4 / Mind 3 / Life 3 / Matter 2 attack that would instantly kill us. However, with assistants in the form of Path of Conjuration 5, or Asymmetrical Reproduction giving us offensive countermagick, we shouldn't have any issues against a ludicrously high success effect .<br /> <br /> Anyways, Horrid Reality will beat any Mage that doesn't have Mind 5, as according to the crossover rules, Spheres and Disciplines must be the same level to directly defend against one another, thus, although they could counterspell us theoretically, they can't have a 100 success Mind 1 shield prepared to negate our successes without Mind 5. Now what can we do against that Mage with Mind 5. Well, honestly, there isn't much. I think that in such a situation, either unweaving (which I'm not entirely sure Night-Folk can do) or another much more insane idea would be our only hope.<br /> <br /> The final insane idea against such a magus would be to get into a fight with a Rank 5 Ananasi werespider beforehand, and get a DNA sample, in order to clone them with Asymmetrical Reproduction so that they can cast Shattering (Rank 5 Gift) that INSTANTLY NEGATES any supernatural effect, including Time hanging spells, and a Mind shield with 100+ successes upon it. Then we can just cast Horrid Reality and win.<br /> <br /> Hope you had a good time reading this insane post lmao.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26413,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","user":"ThatOneKiasyd","date":". 08-13-2022, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T20:09:11-07:00","id":1490086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489046-overpowered-theoretical-in-clan-discipline-combinations?p=1490074#post1490074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope you had a good time reading this insane post lmao.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ladies and gentlemen, we have a Winner!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T17:49:34-07:00","id":1490203,"title":"","content":"There's a few notations that I should make. <br /> <br /> 1. If Perdo Magica from the Players Guide to Low Clans works on Sphere effects (it is only stated to work on Pillars from DA: Mage, but a DM could interpret it as working against Spheres as they're the modern equivalent), then no weird Ananasi play is required, as you can just REFLEXIVELY spend 1 bp and roll Willpower to negate a spell effect (1:1 success ratio, but since it's reflexive you can just cast it as much as you want), therefore being able to rapidly unweave just about anything,<br /> <br /> 2. If you have enough time and energy you can create clones of yourself with Asymmetrical Reproduction and use Power of the Pyramid for insane Willpower bonuses, making ridiculous 100+ success Mage damage reducing shields meaningless against your Theft of Vitae / Cauldron of Blood, as you'll just roll more successes lol. <br /> <br /> 3. I forget if Time 4 effects can be hung before or after they're cast. If a Mage can cast ritual levels of successes to go off immediately due to Time 4, then yeah lots of offensive countermagick (or Shattering) will be needed, but if it's just the one Arete roll after the time trigger goes off, then no more than 10 dice are being rolled, and so you could probably counterspell it alone honestly. <br /> <br /> 4. Changeling Time Realm trigger effects are really annoying, the main offender being Pyretics 5 allowing self-revive, however if you just kill them before they can re-cast it again, you'll avoid any immortal shenanigans they can do. Also, Wayfare teleportation is quite a problem, however you can reasonably just have a Lune or something bound with Spirit Manipulation and force it to open up a Moon Bridge to them or use Path of Mars, etc... Worst case scenario they get away, but you still won that fight, and any residual Chimera you've (unintentionally) created with Chimerstry will make it so they'll never want to come back. <br /> <br /> 5. The Silver Fangs have a Rank 5 Gift, Paws of the Newborn Cub, that allow them to remove all supernatural abilities from a target, again, we win initiative, so it's not a problem. (Speaking of which you could always clone one of them instead of the Ananasi). Same goes for Shattering from the Ananasi, we win initiative so it's not a problem. <br /> <br /> 6. Use Paper Flesh if you're ever in a fight with an Antediluvian with Fortitude 10, I wouldn't know why you would be lmao, but if you are, it'll prevent them from being immune to all damage with Plot Device. <br /> <br /> 7. For elder stuff, which is honestly unnecessary lol, Thaumaturgy 7 lets you turn yourself into a werewolf with Shadow of the Wolf ritual, I don't know what you'd want to do with this, but that Silver Fang Gift I was talking about sounds pretty good. Chimerstry 9 is the best attack in the game even though it's costly, as nothing can stop unsoakable aggravated &quot;reality negation&quot; damage, I can't imagine any Sphere covers that in terms of damage reducing effects. Temporis gets pretty good as you can rewind time, in case you get into a fight before you've prepped. Finally the Loom of Vishnu Sadhana level 6 ritual, which you can get thanks to Rites of the Blood, makes you God in a given area. Do with this what you will. <br /> <br /> 8. Since it's technically RAW, although I try my best to stay away from this, creating your own Thaumaturgy Path to more easily counter the magics of other supernaturals is a good use of that feature, however I specifically did not mention this in my prior post as I was trying to highlight the pre-existing power of the Discipline, even though this &quot;feature&quot; makes Thaumaturgy just that much better. <br /> <br /> 9. If anyone tries this ever, their ST will burn their character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T22:27:48-07:00","id":1490217,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy 5 &amp; Obfuscate 5<br /> <br /> You use Path of Conjuring rank three (can make a modern smart phone) to create <u><b>Tactical</b></u> grade nukes (1950s &amp; 1960s grade technology / backpack sized), scatter them throughout a city, use Obfuscate to avoid confrontation until you can leave the city, then use Path of Technomancy rank four Remote Access to trigger the nukes. Path of Technomancy also means you pretty much turn a city surveillance system into your way of confirming your targets presence and being in weapons range.<br /> <br /> Since the blasts are practically instantaneous there is no option to activate defenses in response to it, and since the Thaumaturge can trigger this from anywhere in the world, there is no way to cancel their actions or counter initiative due to being in an unknown location. Likewise, the Obfuscate prevents direct counters since they can't find you to fight you.<br /> <br /> Lastly in both W:tA and KotE, nuclear/atomic weapons regardless of size do damage to the spirit world on a permanent level, so being immaterial, out of phase, or in a different dimension isn't going to protect you from the blast. If the target somehow survives the initial blast, chances are that the radiation damage will take its toll, even on an undead, based on the mechanics for the Scorpion Eaters Dharma and what happens to normal supernaturals consuming/exposed to tainted energy.<br /> <br /> This approach would only fail against mages who are paranoid enough to consider WMD attacks to take out a single opponent valid and prepare accordingly with some form of automatic teleportation and heavily warded super bunker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T22:37:20-07:00","id":1490218,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, if you really want to mess with an enemy, try this trick.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy 5 and Dominate 5<br /> <br /> Path of Conjuring: Make a living duplicate of yourself, create a bomb vest with a delay timer on a dead man's switch.<br /> <br /> Dominate to use Possession so you inhabit your own mortal shell.<br /> <br /> Then just make a run at your enemy, just before getting in melee range you jump out of the shell, they &quot;kill&quot; your shell and get blown up by the bomb vest. Best case scenario your enemy is dead, worst case they are badly damaged and pretty sure you are dead with very little left to investigate.<br /> <br /> Or you could just keep making these things over and over until the enemy is dead. It is basically Altered Carbon for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}